I was partway through parsing a `let` expression, but I got stuck here:

74|  , ("each stream may carry other cached original revision",let gf={fresh|legacyRevision=original.legacyRevision,legacyRead=original.legacyRead}
75|                                                          lf={fresh|geometryRevision=original.geometryRevision,geometryRead=original.geometryRead}
                                                             ^
Based on the indentation, I was expecting to see the in keyword next. Is there a
